From d4eac39254d84e174ef7ab8083901599443324d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Lui, Jonathan" <jonathan.ming.jun.lui@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 17:54:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/17] media: i2c: ar0234: restore reset GPIO direction on
 resume

The reset GPIO direction may be incorrect after the sensor returns from S3.
Set it back to output before powering on the sensor.

Signed-off-by: Lui, Jonathan <jonathan.ming.jun.lui@intel.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ar0234.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ar0234.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ar0234.c
index 066c5444d4e0..c5acb415dc20 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ar0234.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ar0234.c
@@ -1207,6 +1207,8 @@ static int __maybe_unused ar0234_resume(struct device *dev)
 	mutex_lock(&ar0234_mutex);
 
 	if (ar0234->reset_gpio) {
+		gpiod_direction_output(ar0234->reset_gpio, 0);
+
 		for (count = 0; count < AR0234_PM_MAX_RETRY; count++) {
 			gpiod_set_value_cansleep(ar0234->reset_gpio, 0);
 			msleep(AR0234_REG_SLEEP_200MS);
-- 
2.43.0

